ZSNES 2 desktop audio
=====================

On the maintainer's Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble) system, ZSNES 2.2.3 (i386)
was the last known-good release for audio. Playback worked with the
default SDL3 backend without forcing libao. SDL3 selected its system
audio driver automatically, and the launcher did not force PulseAudio.
The regression appeared after 2.2.3 and was present in 2.3.4. The first
affected release and the cause are unknown.

With 2.3.4 and PipeWire 1.0.5 on that system, the default audio selection
used SDL3 and playback stuttered. Forcing SDL3's PulseAudio driver also
stuttered. Selecting either the native PipeWire backend or SDL3's
PipeWire driver produced no sound. Playback through libao's PulseAudio
output worked on the same system.

The package provides three desktop launchers so users can play with
the working audio path and compare backends when testing the regression.

- "ZSNES 2" defaults to libao's PulseAudio output (-ad ao:pulse).
- "ZSNES 2 (SDL3/PulseAudio)" forces SDL3's PulseAudio driver
  (SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER=pulseaudio with -ad sdl).
- "ZSNES 2 (Native PipeWire)" selects the emulator's native PipeWire
  backend (-ad pipewire).

To try the native PipeWire backend from a terminal, run

    zsnes2 -ad pipewire
